  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Homological Algebra of Knots and BPS States — It is known that knot homologies admit a physical description as spaces of open BPS states. We study operators and algebras acting on these spaces.\n\n**Homological Algebra of Knots and BPS States**\n\n*Sergei Gukov and Marko Stoˇsić*\n\n46 pp, 12 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** It is known that knot homologies admit a physical description as spaces of open BPS states. We study operators and algebras acting on these spaces. This leads to a very rich story, which involves wall crossing phenomena, algebras of closed BPS states acting on spaces of open BPS states, and deformations of Landau-Ginzburg models. One important application to knot homologies is the existence of “colored diﬀerentials” that relate homological invariants of knots colored by diﬀerent representations. Based on this structure, we formulate a list of properties of the colored HOMFLY homology that categoriﬁes the colored HOMFLY polynomial. By calculating the colored HOMFLY homology for symmetric and anti-symmetric representations, we ﬁnd a remarkable “mirror symmetry” between these triply-graded theories.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1 Setting the stage; 2 Algebra of BPS states and its representation; 3 B-model and matrix factorizations; 4 Colored HOMFLY homology; 5 Mirror symmetry for knots; 6 Unreduced colored HOMFLY homology; Appendix A. Notations; Appendix B. Kauffman and S2 homologies of the ; Appendix C. H3 homology of the figure-eight kn; Appendix D. Computation of the unreduced homol; References",
      "lang": "en",
